# Anchored to the repo root, unlike the rest of this block. A bare `lib/` matches a directory
# named `lib` at *any* depth, which silently ignored `application/frontend/src/lib/` — the
# frontend's own library folder, holding htmlBlocks.ts, streaming.ts, exportAsset.ts and the
# rest. Those files are in git only because they were committed before this rule arrived;
# anything added to that folder afterwards was invisible to `git status` and would have been
# missing from a fresh clone. Python's own `lib/` artifacts only ever appear at the root (a
# venv's is already covered by `.venv/`), so anchoring loses nothing.
/lib/
/lib64/
parts/
sdist/
var/
wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg
.pytest_cache/

